he second floor of a purpose-built development, the property offers approximately 620 sq ft of accommodation. The spacious reception room is a particular highlight, with a large window bringing in plenty of natural light and ample room for comfortable seating and a dining table. Wood-effect flooring and neutral décor create a welcoming setting for relaxing at home or entertaining friends.<br /><br />The separate fitted kitchen provides a practical layout with a range of wall and base units, generous worktop space, an integrated oven and gas hob. Having the kitchen separate from the reception room gives the apartment a useful distinction between cooking, dining and relaxing.<br /><br />The main bedroom is a comfortable double, benefiting from mirrored wardrobes and a large window. A second bedroom offers flexibility for those needing a guest room, a child’s bedroom or a dedicated home office. Completing the accommodation is a tiled bathroom with a white suite, a bath with an overhead shower and a glass shower screen.<br /><br />An allocated parking space adds further convenience, particularly for anyone wanting to enjoy the area’s transport connections while keeping a car close to home.<br /><br />Campbell Close is well positioned for Streatham High Road, where an extensive choice of cafés, restaurants, shops and supermarkets makes everyday living straightforward. Whether you are picking up your morning coffee, meeting friends for dinner or doing the weekly shop, there is plenty to enjoy locally.<br /><br />Streatham station is within easy reach, providing rail connections into London and making the location appealing to commuters. Bus services along Streatham High Road offer further options for travelling around South London.<br /><br />The area also offers plenty beyond the commute. Streatham Common provides open space for walks, exercise and relaxing outdoors, while the attractive Rookery gardens offer a lovely setting for a quieter weekend wander. Tooting Common 